     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Having to: «it is necessary for me»",
     "texto": [
      "To say «have to», **надо + infinitive** is used; the person is in the dative: **Мне надо работать** = I have to work (literally, «to me it is necessary to work»).",
      "**Тебе надо** = you have to. **Вам надо** can mean you have to (formal) or you (plural) have to."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Knowing how",
     "texto": [
      "**Уметь + infinitive** expresses knowing how to do something or having a skill: **Я умею плавать** (I can swim), **я умею водить машину** (I can drive).",
      "**Знать** means to know a fact or to be acquainted with; **уметь** means to have the skill to do something. **Мочь** expresses ability or possibility in a situation."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Allowed and not allowed",
     "texto": [
      "You already know **можно**, which expresses permission («it is allowed»). **Нельзя** expresses prohibition («it is not allowed»): **Здесь нельзя курить** = smoking is not allowed here.",
      "**Почему?** = why? **Потому что** = because. **Тогда** = then."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
